cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pastry, please cite it as below, together with the method papers relevant to your application."
title: "pastry: population and hierarchical inference with PDFs"
abstract: >-
  pastry infers population distributions over bins, and the posteriors of
  individual objects, from heteroscedastic per-object likelihoods, posteriors
  or posterior samples, using an exact hierarchical Bayesian model with
  smoothness priors, selection effects and built-in validation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Speagle
    given-names: Joshua S.
version: 0.1.0.dev0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshspeagle/pastry"
keywords:
  - Bayesian inference
  - hierarchical models
  - population inference
  - deconvolution
  - Dirichlet
  - photometric redshifts
  - unfolding
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Hierarchical Bayesian inference of galaxy redshift distributions from photometric surveys"
    authors:
